Wait, they talk now? is MIT-licensed (LICENSE).

It runs on and is built against:
- Fabric Loader and Fabric API (FabricMC), Apache-2.0.
- Minecraft (Mojang): this mod adds no block, item, or entity of its own at this stage. The
  Modrinth listing icon (`docs/modrinth/icon.png`) is a render of vanilla's own villager head
  texture (`minecraft:villager`, `assets/minecraft/textures/entity/villager/villager.png`),
  composed onto the plain cubealgos navy badge (no grid -- this mod is not a Create Fly add-on)
  at build time by `tools/icon.py` from a local Minecraft client jar; no asset file is copied
  into this repo, only the rendered composite `icon.png` (`just icon`).

Piper TTS (github.com/rhasspy/piper, archived, MIT — the frozen snapshot, not the actively
maintained GPL-3.0 `OHF-Voice/piper1-gpl` fork) generates the villager voice lines: a build-time
tool only, never invoked, bundled, or reachable at runtime (`docs/spec/domains/audio.md`
`AUDIO-REQ-005`). Candidate voice models under evaluation for the timbre sample round
(`tools/voices/VOICES.md` has the full licence record):
- `en_US-joe-medium` (dataset: OHF-Voice/voice-datasets), CC0.
- `en_US-kristin-medium` (dataset: LibriVox), public domain.
- `en_US-norman-medium` (dataset: LibriVox), public domain.

Once Kevin approves a sample timbre and the full 64-line batch replaces the placeholder audio, this
credit narrows to the one approved model and this notice discloses the shipped audio as
AI-generated (`docs/spec/operations/compliance.md`, `REL-REQ-004`). NeoForge's own credit is added
once its module lands and its licence is verified (`docs/spec/operations/compliance.md`).
The alpha's 64 shipped sound files are build-generated near-silent placeholder audio (a very soft
click, not true digital silence, `docs/spec/domains/audio.md` `AUDIO-REQ-002`) — not speech, not
AI-generated, and not sourced from anywhere: nothing here is a disclosure obligation yet
(`docs/spec/operations/release.md` `REL-REQ-004`). Piper (voice synthesis, build-time only, never
invoked at runtime) and its voice model will be added and credited here once real audio lands
(`VV-11`, `docs/spec/domains/audio.md`); that credit will also disclose the shipped audio as
AI-generated from that release onward (`docs/spec/operations/compliance.md`). NeoForge's own
credit is added once its module lands and its licence is verified
(`docs/spec/operations/compliance.md`).

All shipped line text and audio are original to this project, never third-party content
(`docs/spec/decisions/DEC-003-licence.md`).
